<title>USA: CBOE, PCX to trade Ascend LEAPS.</title>
<headline>CBOE, PCX to trade Ascend LEAPS.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange and the Pacific Exchange said Friday they would list long-term equity anticipation securities (LEAPS) on shares of Ascend Communications Inc on April 14.</p>
<p>The exchanges said Ascend LEAPS would open with strike prices of 30, 45 and 60 and expirations in January 1998 and January 1999.</p>
<p>Ascend shares were down 3-3/8 at 43 Friday afternoon.</p>
<p>The American Stock Exchange said Thursday it would trade Ascend LEAPS.</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
